  "_howto": "Add a card: copy its CardTrader (or Cardmarket) URL, paste as `url`, give it a `group` (card name), a `variant` (printing) and a `code` (official Scryfall set code, shown in the Set column at every width). language defaults to defaultLanguage. Cardmarket URLs need `?language=7` (Japanese) — the site filters there, not via `language`. Two Cardmarket URL shapes, pick per card. ALL-VERSIONS (/Magic/Cards/<Card-Name>) covers every printing in one scrape — cheapest when you genuinely want them all; mark it allVersions: true with variant \"All printings\" and no code. PER-PRINTING (/Magic/Products/Singles/<Set>/<Card>) is right when only certain printings matter — a fetchland's all-versions page is mostly reprints you do not watch, and a per-printing entry also carries its own set code so the Set column is correct. Same cost per scrape either way. CardTrader has no all-versions equivalent, so it always needs one URL per printing.",
  "_cardmarket": "Cardmarket is scraped ONLY on demand (the site's button, or Actions -> Run workflow) through Firecrawl, which bills credits per scrape. Spending is controlled by CREDITS, not by a scrape count: each run may spend remaining balance / days left in the billing period, minus what today already cost, and never dips into cardmarketMinCredits. cardmarketMonthlyCredits only paces things when the API reports no billing period. The TTL, per-run limit and scrape-count fallback still exist in cloud/fetch-cardmarket.js as defaults, but every real run sends force=true and so bypasses them — they were removed from here rather than left looking like live settings. cardmarketCountry is the country Firecrawl browses from.",
